# Integration roadmap (Linear)

When implementing integrations, agents-as-workers, or workflow execution, follow the prioritized backlog:

**Master doc:** `docs/integration/LINEAR_INTEGRATION_BACKLOG.md`

- **Tier 1 (30 days):** Platform foundation + HubSpot + handoffs — Linear STA-6 through STA-23
- **Tier 2 (90 days):** Salesforce, Finance, DevOps, Marketing analytics, knowledge sync — STA-24 through STA-49
- **Tier 3 (6 months):** NetSuite, Workday, LinkedIn SN, Marketo, Segment, marketplace SDK — STA-50 through STA-73
- **Tier 4 (12 months):** Compliance, VPC/white-label, extended HR/finance, AI governance, HA, marketplace v2 — STA-74 through STA-99
- **Tier 5 (18 months):** Auto-execute agents, regulated verticals, B2B federation, swarms, platform intelligence — see backlog doc

Do not start Tier 2 connector work until Tier 1 **invoke_tool** (STA-10) and **merge execution engines** (STA-12) are done unless the issue explicitly says otherwise.

Do not start Tier 3 until Tier 1 platform and relevant Tier 2 connector patterns are shipped.

Do not start Tier 4 until Tier 3 marketplace foundation (STA-70, STA-73) for ecosystem epics.

Do not start Tier 5 auto-execute (Epic A) until Tier 1–4 guardrails (STA-10, STA-11, STA-82, STA-90) are shipped.

After completing a Linear issue, update its status in Linear and note blockers for dependent issues in the backlog doc if scope changed.
